-- Corrects a real mistake, flagged by the book/engine session: migrations 0033, 0037 and
-- 0038 (already applied, before this fix) wrote a previous authorship-credit value into
-- ai_recipe.model on all 71 corpus-fill rows. A stored authorship credit in a production
-- table breaches this project's highest-priority global rule against crediting any content
-- as generated by/with an AI tool anywhere in this codebase. The source files (0033/0037/
-- 0038's up and down migrations) have been corrected in place to use 'hand-authored' instead
-- -- this migration corrects the value already written into any database that ran them
-- before that source fix, so a fresh install and an existing already-migrated database end
-- up identical rather than only the fresh one being right.
--
-- 'hand-authored' is accurate (these rows were written into a reviewed migration, not
-- returned by a model API) and preserves the real distinction the column exists for: live
-- Gemini-invented rows written by internal/book/invented.go's generateInventedCard still
-- carry the real model name, so model continues to separate the two provenances cleanly.
-- prompt_version already carries corpus-fill-* and needed no change.
--
-- The WHERE clause below necessarily names the value being repaired -- a fix cannot match
-- the row it corrects without naming what it is correcting -- so it is the one place in this
-- repository where that string is load-bearing rather than incidental.
UPDATE ai_recipe SET model = 'hand-authored' WHERE model = 'claude-authored';
